{title: Green Olive Tree}
{subtitle: Psalms 52:10}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 83}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] | [Bb] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]God will tear you down forev[Eb]er
[Bb]Snatch you from your tent and [Eb]land
[Gm]Uprooted from the living ground
[F]Your strength is built on wicked [Eb]ways
[Bb]Trusted in your [Eb]great wealth
[Bb]Refused to make God [Eb]your refuge
[Gm]The righteous see and stand in [F]awe
Laughing at your hollow [Eb]pride
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
But I am like a [Bb]green olive [Eb]tree
In the house of God I [Gm]stand
[Eb]I trust in [Bb]God's mercy forev[Eb]er
Steady in his [Gm]gra[F]cious [Eb]hand
Like a green olive [Gm]tree
[F]In the house of God I [Bb]am [Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]The man who trusted in his [Eb]coin
[Bb]Grew strong in his own [Eb]deceit
[Gm]But the righteous watch his [F]fall
Awe and laughter fill the [Eb]air
[Bb]He had no refuge in the [Eb]Lord
[Bb]Only his own wic[Eb]ked might
[Gm]Now the tent is torn [F]away
Up from the land of [Eb]living
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
But I am like a [Bb]green olive [Eb]tree
In the house of God I [Gm]stand
[Eb]I trust in God's [Bb]mercy forev[Eb]er
Steady in his [Gm]gra[F]cious [Eb]hand
Like a green olive [Gm]tree
[F]In the house of God I [Bb]am
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]I will praise you forev[F]er
[Gm]Because you have acted [F]good
[Eb]In the presence of your faith[F]ful
[Gm]Hope remains in your [Eb]name
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Green olive [Bb]tree in his [Eb]house
Mercy [Bb]forever [Eb]and ev[Bb]er
{end_of_verse}

